    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.15) and **James Wood** (73.49) serving as our primary anchors. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a highly favorable matchup against Bibee, where a 14% boost from dynamic platoon optimization cements his status as our most efficient start. Similarly, **James Wood** capitalizes on an elite 0.404 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot, making him the highest-projected outfield asset. **Corbin Carroll** and **Josh Naylor** also provide significant upside; despite the slight drag on **Corbin Carroll**'s score due to elite hold-runners (SP vs SB), his speed profile remains a mandatory lock for our stolen base pursuit. We are also leaning into the platoon advantage for **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 65.80 is bolstered by a 14% dynamic platoon bump, keeping him comfortably in the lineup despite a lower batting order position.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision today involved **Griffin Conine**, who fell just short of the starting threshold with a score of 34.07. While **Griffin Conine** offers power, the combination of a difficult matchup against Suter and a stagnant platoon disadvantage pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency floor. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Jose Caballero**, many of whom remain sidelined or unavailable. With **Brice Turang** and **Travis Bazzana** rounding out the middle infield, we are maintaining a disciplined approach to our game caps; we are prioritizing the high-floor production of **Isaac Paredes** and **Gabriel Moreno** against their respective right-handed matchups while keeping the bench thin to ensure we aren't burning starts on low-probability outcomes.",
